                        "name": "Sridevi Ramesh",
                        "email": "sridevra@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SrideviRamesh"
                    },
                    "message": "I executed this test in our environment.\n\nHere, the BMC has two sides running, backup image. Via GUI the running image is fetched which is correct.\n\nBut, via redfish there no validation on which side is the ${redfish_firmware} is fetched.\n\n```\ncurl -k -H \"X-Auth-Token: $bmc_token\" -X GET https://${bmc}/redfish/v1/UpdateService/FirmwareInventory\n{\n  \"@odata.id\": \"/redfish/v1/UpdateService/FirmwareInventory\",\n  \"@odata.type\": \"#SoftwareInventoryCollection.SoftwareInventoryCollection\",\n  \"Members\": [\n    {\n      \"@odata.id\": \"/redfish/v1/UpdateService/FirmwareInventory/1bcff1f5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"@odata.id\": \"/redfish/v1/UpdateService/FirmwareInventory/b5478144\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"Members@odata.count\": 2,\n  \"Name\": \"Software Inventory Collection\"\n}\n```\n\non running this, observed that backup side is fetched.\n\nCan we get both running & backup images in the tests and verify the both via redfish?? that completes the full validation as well?"
                }
